From: PS5 Proton contributors
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: let the broker present the guest image extent

The broker scales completed linear images in the owner. It has no fixed
native scanout in the child, so forcing the VideoOut fullscreen blit chooses
the minimum supported size (1x1) instead of the window's image extent.
Keep the existing fixed-display path for ordinary titles.

--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -3072,6 +3072,8 @@ static BOOL surface_get_fshack_dpi( struct surface *surface )
 {
     UINT dpi = NtUserGetDpiForWindow( surface->hwnd ), raw = NtUserGetWinMonitorDpi( surface->hwnd, MDT_RAW_DPI );
 #ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    const char *broker = getenv( "WINE_PS5_GPU_BROKER" );
+    if (broker && broker[0] == '1' && !broker[1]) return 0;
     /* VideoOut has one fixed scanout extent, even when Windows DPI matches.
      * Render at the guest extent and use Proton's existing presentation blit. */
     return raw ? raw : USER_DEFAULT_SCREEN_DPI;
